scope.summary:
GOAL: Implement the in-process session event bus: a tokio::sync::broadcast fan-out publishing lifecycle/turn/steer/ack events for concurrent consumers (GUI panes, orchestrator notification, recording), with persisted-event correlation ids so any bus consumer can join durable rows (ProcessOwnershipLedger process_uuid, agent_session_* revisions, FR trace ids), bounded buffers, and EXPLICIT lag handling — a slow subscriber must observe a typed gap marker, never silent loss (HBR-SWARM-002). Pattern precedent: BroadcastSwarmSink already does broadcast fan-out for SwarmEvent (src/backend/handshake_core/src/swarm_orchestration/events.rs lines 452-486: tokio broadcast sender, new(capacity.max(1)), subscribe()); this bus is its session-domain sibling with a stronger no-silent-loss contract and correlation-id payloads.

EXPECTED DIFF SHAPE: (a) new file src/backend/handshake_core/src/agent_sessions/bus.rs; (b) pub use in agent_sessions/mod.rs; (c) new test file src/backend/handshake_core/tests/agent_sessions_bus_tests.rs. No changes to swarm_orchestration/events.rs (the SwarmEvent sink stays untouched; a bridging consumer can be added by later families).

SPEC CATALOG:

- pub struct EventCorrelation { pub session_id: SessionId, pub turn_id: Option<TurnId>, pub message_id: Option<SteerMessageId>, pub process_record_id: Option<uuid::Uuid> (the ProcessOwnershipRecordId uuid from the ledger START row — official_cli_bridge.rs mints it at spawn, line 2449), pub fr_trace_id: Option<String> (joins the FR trace stamped per invocation, cli_bridge_runtime.rs lines 663-674), pub store_revision: Option<i64> (the agent_session_* revision the event corresponds to, when the event mirrors a durable write) } — serde; every event carries one; this is the join key surface that makes bus consumers able to reconstruct truth from durable state (HBR-INT-007).
- pub enum SessionBusEvent (serde tag="kind" snake_case, each variant carrying correlation: EventCorrelation + at_utc: DateTime<Utc>):
  ThreadStarted { adapter_kind: AgentAdapterKind, cwd: String, worktree_id: Option<String> };
  TurnStateChanged { from: TurnState, to: TurnState, seq: u32 };
  TurnItemAppended { item_kind: String (the TurnItem serde tag), preview: String (first 200 chars, redaction-safe: previews of ToolCall inputs pass through the existing redactor seam used by the CLI runtime capture path — cli_bridge_runtime.rs AgentCaptureState.redactor lines 755-767 — the bus takes an optional Arc<dyn Fn(&str)->String + Send + Sync> redactor at construction) };
  SteerQueued { depth: usize };
  SteerAckChanged { ack_state: String };
  ResendExhausted {};
  InterruptRequested {};
  SessionHealthChanged { health: String };
  SessionClosed { mapped_thread_state: String, exit_code: Option<i32> };
  SubscriberLagged { missed: u64 } — SYNTHESIZED per-subscriber (see lag rule), never published by producers.
- pub struct SessionEventBus { tx: tokio::sync::broadcast::Sender<SessionBusEvent>, lag_counter: Arc<AtomicU64>, capacity: usize } : pub fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self (default pub const SESSION_BUS_CAPACITY: usize = 1024; capacity.max(1) like BroadcastSwarmSink); pub fn publish(&self, event: SessionBusEvent) -> usize (returns receiver count; a publish with zero receivers is fine — durable state is the source of truth, the bus is a live-delta channel); pub fn subscribe(&self) -> SessionBusSubscriber.
- pub struct SessionBusSubscriber { rx: broadcast::Receiver<SessionBusEvent>, bus_lag_counter: Arc<AtomicU64> } : pub async fn recv(&mut self) -> Option<SessionBusEvent> — LAG RULE (normative): on RecvError::Lagged(n), increment the shared lag counter AND return Some(SessionBusEvent::SubscriberLagged { missed: n }) with a correlation carrying only session-less bus identity — the consumer SEES the gap as a typed event and can re-sync from durable state; on RecvError::Closed return None. Silent skip is forbidden.
- pub fn lag_total(&self) -> u64 on SessionEventBus — diagnostic counter surfaced to the HBR-INT-009 tiers (flight_recorder event on first lag per subscriber window; internal_diagnostics/palmistry wiring may be typed DEFERRED).
- Supervisor/queue/receipt hookup seams (implemented here, consumed by MT-005/MT-007/MT-010): pub struct BusSupervisorHook(Arc<SessionEventBus>) implementing MT-005's SupervisorEventHook by mapping on_health_changed -> SessionHealthChanged and on_exit -> SessionClosed with NON-BLOCKING publish only (broadcast::send never awaits — safe from the supervisor poll thread); helper constructors for SteerQueued/SteerAckChanged events from MT-002/MT-008 outcomes.
- FR bridging: pub struct FlightRecorderBusConsumer — a spawned task subscribing and forwarding SessionClosed/ThreadStarted/SubscriberLagged (and only those three — TurnItemAppended volume is capped out) to the FlightRecorder as events stamping fr_event_id strings "FR-EVT-ASESS-THREAD-STARTED", "FR-EVT-ASESS-SESSION-CLOSED", "FR-EVT-ASESS-SUBSCRIBER-LAGGED" into the payload, following the SELF-CONTAINED constant-table discipline SwarmFrEventId documents (events.rs lines 9-20: FR-EVT-* ids defined product-side as a round-trippable table because .GOV registry folding is a governance-wave concern; MT-161 folds them) — pub enum AgentSessionFrEventId { ThreadStarted, SessionClosed, SubscriberLagged } with as_str()/all()/from_str_id() exactly mirroring SwarmFrEventId (events.rs lines 36-109).

STEP-BY-STEP IMPLEMENTATION:
1. Read swarm_orchestration/events.rs L452-520 (BroadcastSwarmSink + FanoutSwarmSink + FlightRecorderSwarmSink patterns and tests L691-725), cli_bridge_runtime.rs L663-674 (trace ids) and L755-767 (redactor seam), MT-001 types, MT-005 SupervisorEventHook signature, MT-008 AckState labels.
2. Implement EventCorrelation + SessionBusEvent with serde wire-tag pins.
3. Implement SessionEventBus/SessionBusSubscriber with the normative lag rule; unit-test the Lagged synthesis with a capacity-2 bus and a slow consumer.
4. Implement BusSupervisorHook + the ack/queue event helper constructors; document non-blocking-only publishing.
5. Implement AgentSessionFrEventId + FlightRecorderBusConsumer forwarding the three chosen kinds; validate emitted events with FlightRecorderEvent::validate() like the swarm sink test does (events.rs L562-580).
6. Author tests/agent_sessions_bus_tests.rs: (a) multi-subscriber fan-out — 3 subscribers each receive all events in publish order; (b) lag proof — capacity 2, publish 10, slow subscriber receives SubscriberLagged{missed>=1} then subsequent events, lag_total()>0, and the missed count reconciles (received + missed == published); (c) publish with zero subscribers does not error; (d) correlation joins — an event constructed from a fake ledger START row + store revision carries process_record_id + store_revision that match the source rows; (e) FR consumer — the three kinds arrive at a CollectingRecorder-style fake with valid events and pinned fr_event_id strings; TurnItemAppended does NOT arrive; (f) wire-tag pin test for every SessionBusEvent variant; (g) redactor application on TurnItemAppended preview.
7. cargo build + clippy green.
